from richard Frank:
if get a message like: "cannot obtain database info on
this  terminal..." when you try to connect...
  
 cd /etc/auth/system; mv ttys.db ttysdb.bak 

 vi ttys and include info for the terminal(s) you want
to have connect,in this example "aether" is the name
of the PC.

aether\:0|aether\:0.0:t_devname=aether\:0:t_xdisplay:t_login_timeout#0:chkent:

do  /usr/tcb/bin/convauth -dt   to change ttys file to
ttys.db 

***********This worked.***********************

