From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Jul 28 21:23:21 1999
From: Brian Wince <brianw () synacom ! com>
Date: Wed, 28 Jul 1999 21:23:21 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: How to change resolution of 9FX motion card on boot up
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079058316131

My original question:

We have a TRUCluster ASE with two Alphaserver 2100 using a 9FX MOTION 331

card as the console graphics controller. These cards came with the 2100's

when they were purchased. The problem is that we can not use the console

for any of our GUI's because of the resolution that is being selected at

system boot. My question is, is there a way to modify either the kernel or

SRM or in the ECU configuration so that it does not select 640X480 at

system boot. If I look at the /usr/var/adm/messages file it sees the card

as a 9FX motion 331 but says it is selecting 640X480. This card supports

resolution up to 1280X1024.


Thanks to Paul Watson for his reply:


You need to edit the file /usr/dt/config/Xservers in it you will see a line

e.g.


:0Local localconsole /usr/bin/X11/X: 0


if you add


-screen0 800


to the end of this line that will give you 800x600 resolution, obviously your

choice of resolution depends also upon your monitor.


Even though this did not fix ny problem I thought it may be helpful to others.


Well after some digging I finally got to the bottom of this. This cluster is at a remote site and the information I was given was incorrect. This cluster actually has a standard isa vga card installed and Dunix and the console and the card are actually doing what they are supposed to. The 9FX MOTION 331 is actually an S3 trio as far as the kernel is concerned. My only recourse is to purchase a svga graphics card for each system. 

