HI All , 
	Thanks to all the people who wrote and phoned ! . 
	I finally got a couple of engineers from Digital over
	who basically wanted to have a good long play with
	the HSZ22 & SWCC  . Basically the deal is : 

	To upgrade to 2 controllers , you have to insert the first
	controller , and backup its configuration to the PC . 
	You then remove the first controller and put the second
	one in the top slot. You then restore the config from the PC .
	Then you can put the original controller in the bottom slot . 

	The fact of the second controller being greyed out on the
	SWCC tcp/ip conection is correct .
	
	What we found out was that if you failover a controller
	with the PC SWCC GUI , you have to physically pop it 
	out and in to recover it , doing a restart from the GUI
	doesn't work . Also if you refresh the GUI after 
	replacing the controller , it doesn't show the controllers
	as going back to active/active . This is a bug , You have
	to close the GUI down and re-open/connect it to get the 
	correct display . 

	You can connect a second kzpba adapter to the port
	H1 if you want and select target 1 for naming some 
	other disks and use that for load sharing . 



