The original question:
----------------------------------------------------------------------
I have seen several messages from people having this same problem, but I
can't find someone who sent a solution to it.
We have an alpha running DU v4.0D + patchset 3. We are having a problem
using dtmail. The user get's an error such as:

  "Cannot set owner of temporary mailbox file.
   Temporary Mailbox file: /usr/spool/mail/joe tmp.379774fa
   Owner uid requested: 1333
   Reason: Not owner"

  The /var/spool/mail directory is nfs mounted from another machine.
No other mailers have this problem however.
-------------------------------------------------------------------

  I had several replies which suggested I set the group of /var/spool/mail
to the mail group. I did this and dtmail now works. 
I also got a reply from Dr. Thomas P. Blinn saying this was
probably a dtmail bug.
All messages are included below. Thanks for the quick help!

