>The  problem with dtmail arises because 
>Digital Unix implements the 'chown' command 
>differently than the Sun Solaris operating system 
>does, and Sun Microsystems wrote the dtmail software.
>
>Apparently, the 'workaround' (no solution)
>is to change the group ownership of the file 
>/var/spool/mail to be 'mail'.
>
>I have done this:
>   prompt> pwd
>   /var/spool
>   prompt> ls -la
>   drwxrwxrwt   2 root     mail        8192 Jun 10 06:23 mail

>A second 'workaround' is to change the group ownership of
>the file /var/spool/mail/specific_user to the same group 
>ownership (whatever it is) as the file /var/spool/mail.

