From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Jul 22 02:21:14 1999
From: "Ronald D. Bowman" <rdbowma () tsi ! clemson ! edu>
Date: Thu, 22 Jul 1999 02:21:14 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: summary: cde calendar hangs
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079058315976

I finally took some time and solved my problem.  If I had
taken a little more time back when I wrote the initial
problem, i had the solution at hand.

paraphrased question - the CDE calendar DTCM process would run
for an hour or so when I logged in.  It would then create a
135 meg core file. 

Solution: There was a lock file in /var/spool/calendar
under the name .lock.tsi

I did not see the file since it started with a .

I should have known better.  Anyway deleting the
lock file solved my problem.

Ron

