Thank you for your replies especially
Simon Greaves
Tony JmcGovern
which by parts lead me to the solution. My problem was that the nics =
where not connected to rest of the
net during configuration. Because I just wanted to set it up and test =
it, I used a address on the same subnet. Then the netsetup procedure put =
the default gateway onto the newly configured (not connected) nic -- (I =
don't know how to avoid this - if you want to setup special routes to =
share the net load to several nics, you may want several nics in the =
same subnet, but maybe not to have the default gateway on any arbitrary =
nic ) -- and the system hung during nis invoke.

Regards,

Rudi Gabler

