Subject: SUMMARY: Firmware level ??
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079058315829

Thanks very much to all who replied.  There were so many replies, I've created
a short precis below:

1) use uerf: ie  uerf -R -r 300 |pg
 This will scan the binary error log for any startup operations (300's) and
print them in reverse order ie last first (-R).

2) use sys_check: ie sys_check -config > systemname.html

3) use decevent ie dia -i configurations|more

4) check recent boot messages in /var/adm/messages

5) check the last config entry in /var/adm/binary.errlog

6) if you have it, run the consvar program: ie consvar -v -l

The reason for the original email query was due to my confusion apon reading
that I needed to have A11 or
firmware when using KZPSA I/O adapters and patchkit 3 for DU3.0D.
If anyone is interested that information is also available in uerf -R
-r300|more.  Look  for your KZPSA adapter as
pza0 and it will mention a firmware version for that adapter.

Thanks again to all, Ruth Belin

