From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Jul 07 08:34:55 1999
From: "Thomas.Meyer" <meyert () dla-marbach ! de>
Date: Wed, 07 Jul 1999 08:34:55 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: giving eXcursion Apps another font to start with
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079058315727

Our question was:

  Dear tru(e) 64 managers (there are certainly more than that out
  there),

  we are looking for a possibility to start e.g. xterm as an eXcursion
  3.0 application using a non default font (i.e. other that "fixed",
  which is not capable of dealing with umlauts) and are facing the
  following problems:

  A natural choice would be to define an eXcursion app like this one:

  /usr/bin/X11/xterm -fn -adobe-*-medium-r-*-*-14-720-0-*-m-*-iso8859-1=

  -sb -sl 255 -ls -ti HOSTNAME

  Unfortunately this will end with a GPF:

  LAUNCH verursachte einen Fehler durch eine ung=FCltige Seite
  in Modul LAUNCH.EXE bei 0137:0040d3e7.
  ...

  We tried to define the font via .Xdefaults or via
  /usr/lib/X11/app-defaults, but to no avail.

  Any help is very much appreciated.

There was no answer, but we found the solution ourselves, partly
through an article in the c't magazine 12/99.

a) personal setting

If you wish to change the default font only for yourself, edit
.Xdefaults in your home directory and add a line like this one:

xterm *Font: -adobe-*-bold-r-*-*-14-720-0-*-m-*-iso8859-1

b) global setting

All users are affected if you modify /usr/lib/X11/app-defaults/XTerm

In our case, we added the following line:

HOST:/usr/lib/X11/app-defaults# diff XTerm.orig  XTerm=20=20=20=20=20
76a77
> *vt100.font:          -adobe-*-medium-r-*-*-14-720-0-*-m-*-iso8859-1
HOST:/usr/lib/X11/app-defaults#=20

You can use resedit to find the appropriate names for widget
propeties.

Other Applications could be modified accordingly.

